#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:12
msgid "Capabilities and mechanisms"
msgstr "Képességek és mechanizmusok"

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:14
msgid ""
"Post-filing reconciliation compares a work unit and its persisted "
"calculation against either a local AEAT justificante PDF or a filed "
"declaration PDF. Both paths check modelo, period, exercise year, and "
"active-profile tax identifier. Justificantes also compare the printed "
"payment/refund total with the registry-declared result casilla and its "
"tolerance. A missing comparison target, persisted revision, receipt "
"total, or identity anchor is recorded as an advisory; it does not "
"silently convert an identity-only match into a claim that the amount was "
"checked. Parse failures become a typed refusal rather than exposing "
"parser exception text. File and secure-byte entrypoints "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation.py`), shared identity "
"comparison (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation.py`), receipt-"
"total reconciliation (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:16
msgid ""
"Declaration-level comparison is currently enrolled for Modelos 100, 111, "
"130, 190, 303, and 390. Other declaration targets are refused before the "
"PDF is opened. Enrolled cases compare numeric extracted values against "
"the persisted revision using the registry's verification policy: required"
" computed casillas are checked even if absent in the filing, optional "
"`reconcile_when_present` casillas are compared only when present on both "
"sides, and export-exempt or non-printing values are excluded. Decimal and"
" integer observations participate; booleans and text do not. Differences "
"are typed as mismatched, missing-in-filed, or extra-in-filed, sorted "
"deterministically, and value-bearing records require registry legal and "
"source references. Provisional extraction profiles produce a manual-"
"verification advisory. Enrolled model gate "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation.py`), registry-scoped "
"declaration comparison "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation.py`), numeric casilla "
"comparison (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconcile_casilla.py`), "
"grounded persisted diff contract "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_records.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:18
msgid ""
"The local PDF path never contacts AEAT and reads an already-persisted "
"calculation revision rather than recalculating. A second path accepts "
"justificante bytes from a same-profile secure capture and does not write "
"a plaintext file. Both prepare a report, encrypted reconciliation record,"
" and compact `MODELO_RECONCILED` bucket event, then persist the record "
"and event atomically in one unit of work. The detailed record keeps the "
"registry references in force at comparison time; the event keeps verdict "
"and counts, with a visibly shortened evidence path to fit its payload "
"limit. Atomic report/event preparation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation.py`), encrypted record "
"and persistence boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_records.py`), secure "
"justificante pull checks "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_pull_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:20
msgid ""
"Registered operations let an operator import local evidence, reconcile a "
"previously captured justificante, and list reconciliation history. Import"
" and pull resolve the exact profile/work unit, pin the operation "
"authority, and mark a persistence phase uncertain before attempting the "
"atomic write; their public result is released only when its terminal "
"receipt proves a successful update. Pull additionally checks that capture"
" bucket, modelo, year, and period match the selected work unit. The list "
"operation returns a whole-profile or per-work-unit history with verdict, "
"diff count, actor, time, and source path, in canonical order; it does not"
" return the detailed diff rows through this particular projection. Import"
" write and receipt boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_import_operation.py`), "
"pull target matching and persistence "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_pull_operation.py`), "
"history result validation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_list_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:22
msgid ""
"Registry discovery exposes registry-backed model codes, a support matrix,"
" model descriptions, period tokens, casilla lists/details, bindings, and "
"formulas. Queries run through the caller's pinned authority. An `as_of` "
"value is rejected on an unscoped request instead of being accepted and "
"ignored; the filing-year-scoped forms are the ones that can honor "
"historical validity. A shared required-input helper separately defines "
"which manually typed required casillas verification expects, excluding "
"casillas supplied by repeated detail rows. Pinned query boundary and "
"scope guard (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/registry_discovery.py`), "
"registry support matrix "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/registry_discovery.py`), manual-input "
"requirement rule (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/required_inputs.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:24
msgid ""
"Result presentation and filing disposition are kept separate. The "
"headline summary selects result-to-pay/refund totals and key figures from"
" registry verification expectations, emits only values present in the "
"persisted revision, and resolves labels in the requested output language."
" The disposition resolver validates the revision's casilla map against "
"the work unit's selected registry revision before deriving the fichero "
"declaration type. It applies Modelo 303 refund rules and positive-payment"
" choices in one shared result used by export and cross-period carry: "
"REDEME enrollment resolves eligible negative periods to refund; a non-"
"REDEME filer must opt in to refund for the year's final period; "
"unsupported payment choices and ineligible elections refuse. Registry-"
"derived result summary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/result_summary.py`), validated "
"disposition entrypoint "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/result_disposition_resolution.py`), "
"payment and refund election gates "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/result_disposition_resolution.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:26
msgid ""
"Review packages provide an operator-directed accountant handoff. Building"
" one requires a verified-complete or filed revision and a matching work-"
"unit identity and registry coordinate. It bundles the already-rendered "
"fichero bytes, full calculation revision and observations, optional "
"ledger evidence, and a typed package descriptor into a checksum-manifest "
"ZIP. Files are staged in a temporary sibling of the chosen output path, "
"rather than shared OS temp, and the bundle writer performs an atomic "
"final write. Verification checks member integrity and the descriptor, and"
" re-confirms the registry revision. The ZIP is a plaintext shareable "
"export; the checksum says whether members changed, not who created it. "
"Package build gates and contents "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/review_package.py`), staging and "
"verification (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/review_package.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:28
msgid ""
"The counter-sign layer adds independent Ed25519 acknowledgment: an "
"accountant signs the operator's original signature-hex bytes plus a NUL "
"separator and note. Verification rechecks the operator-signed package "
"first, then verifies the counter-signature against a public key supplied "
"by the caller; it does not trust the receipt's embedded counter-key as "
"the trust anchor. Creating a counter-signature does not itself verify the"
" original package signature, so callers that need pre-sign assurance must"
" verify first; the combined verifier rejects an invalid original "
"signature later. Collaboration audit helpers append recipient "
"registration/removal, package-encrypted/decrypted, counter-sign, and "
"attached-feedback events. Decryption gets a privacy event; keys and "
"plaintext bytes are omitted from event payloads. The attached-feedback "
"event refuses unless the imported counter-sign receipt has already been "
"verified. Counter-sign message and creation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/review_package_counter_sign.py`), two-"
"layer verification "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/review_package_counter_sign.py`), "
"collaboration audit events "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/review_package_collab_audit.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:30
msgid "Knowledge, safety, and implementation assessment"
msgstr "Tudás, biztonságosság és megvalósítási értékelés"

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:32
msgid ""
"The sources of truth here are registry-declared casillas, expectations, "
"tolerances, and legal/source references; persisted work revisions and "
"filed observations; the active profile; and secure capture snapshots. The"
" parser and persistence interfaces are ports, so this slice does not "
"establish PDF extraction accuracy or the concrete encryption/storage "
"adapter's implementation. The reconciliation comments identify "
"provisional declaration extraction profiles and the need to manually "
"compare their values against printed documents. The secure-byte path "
"handles justificantes only; filed declarations captured through the "
"separate sweep already have observation values used by the pulled-filing "
"comparison documented in [STAGE-2-080](080-modelo-projections-queries-"
"quickfile-and-recipient-encryption.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:34
msgid ""
"Several boundaries merit cross-module verification. "
"`resolve_modelo_result_disposition` intentionally resolves the registry "
"snapshot using its caller-supplied `period` while the work unit has its "
"own period; its comment says the two are expected to agree but that this "
"boundary does not prove it. Call sites should establish equality before "
"relying on period-sensitive refund eligibility. Reconciliation records "
"retain a full source path while the event shortens it; the whole-profile "
"history projection also publishes that path, so paths containing "
"usernames or private directory names can be disclosed to an authorized "
"reader. Finally, record history rechecks revision carry against current "
"authority; a later registry revision mismatch can make old entries refuse"
" to list, even though the stored record preserves its original grounding."
" Caller-period resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/result_disposition_resolution.py`), full"
" source reference storage "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_records.py`), history "
"carry check (`src/cadrumo/application/modelo/reconciliation_records.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/081-reconciliation-filing-disposition-and-accountant-review-packages.md:36
msgid ""
"The strongest local controls are deterministic registry-scoped "
"comparison, disclosure of unverified anchors and missing totals, "
"mandatory grounding on value diffs, atomic record/event co-write, target "
"checks on secure pulls, and signature verification against independently "
"supplied trust keys. The package builder trusts its caller to supply the "
"correct draft bytes and work unit/revision pair beyond its explicit ID "
"and registry-coordinate checks; export-time eligibility is owned by the "
"upstream exporter. No tests are included among the assigned files, so "
"none of the claimed behavior was exercised in this pass."
msgstr ""

